1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,620
Everyone says that chassis bracing makes a difference.

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:05,500
Today, we're actually going to show you how much of a difference.

3
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:08,220
Numerically and with facts

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:08,880
and data.

5
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:13,960
All cars flex.

6
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:18,120
Every time you take a corner, load travels through the chassis and the body bends.

7
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:22,680
Every bit of chassis flex introduces vagueness into the steering and handling.

8
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:27,080
On an open top car like a Miata, with no roof structure to help resist that flex,

9
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,760
it's even more pronounced.

10
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:31,260
In theory, chassis bracing fixes this.

11
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:34,840
It adds stiffness, reduces flex, and sharpens the handling,

12
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:37,720
which is especially important when you're chasing lap times.

13
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:39,320
But does it actually work?

14
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:41,800
And is it quantifiably measurable?

15
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:43,400
If so, how much?

16
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:46,280
Today, we're going to find out with actual data.

17
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:51,160
Part of what we got were actually these fender braces we got from Goodwin Racing.

18
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:52,280
Thank you, Goodwin.

19
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:57,000
As well as this strut tower brace from Whiteline Performance.

20
00:00:57,020 --> 00:00:59,400
These are both NA and NB Miata fitment.

21
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:04,600
So we're going to go ahead and throw these on the car in a very controlled test.

22
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:07,320
Strut tower braces are such an easy mod and everyone does it.

23
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:09,000
How much does it work exactly?

24
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,720
Everyone says it works like they can feel the difference.

25
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:13,080
But can we measure the difference?

26
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:16,040
Can we actually see how much it does numerically?

27
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:17,720
And since we have scanning data,

28
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:20,780
I realized we have a way to actually measure it and show the world

29
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:23,260
just how much it changes the car.

30
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:25,960
We can't use Grimace, unfortunately.

31
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:27,400
Grimace has a cage in it.

32
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:30,280
The cage makes the car significantly stiffer than factory.

33
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:32,920
And most of these guys are going to be doing these on factory cars.

34
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:34,620
So first, we're going to need a stock car.

35
00:01:38,541 --> 00:01:40,701
Welcome to our neighbors.

36
00:01:41,341 --> 00:01:43,181
This is Miata Chop Shop.

37
00:01:43,821 --> 00:01:46,621
Because our Miata is caged and is a race car,

38
00:01:47,901 --> 00:01:50,761
in order to give you what we really want to show you

39
00:01:50,781 --> 00:01:53,081
on the fender bracing and the strut tower bracing,

40
00:01:53,101 --> 00:01:54,541
we wanted to use a stock car.

41
00:01:55,101 --> 00:01:57,321
So most kits will fit NA and NB.

42
00:01:57,341 --> 00:02:00,441
So we're going to use this clean stock NB1

43
00:02:00,461 --> 00:02:02,361
as kind of our reference car.

44
00:02:02,381 --> 00:02:05,321
So big thanks to our buddies at Miata Chop Shop.

45
00:02:05,341 --> 00:02:06,361
If you want to take a look,

46
00:02:06,381 --> 00:02:08,221
they do a whole bunch of Miata part-outs.

47
00:02:09,341 --> 00:02:12,441
Everything in here, all the parts you could ever need.

48
00:02:12,461 --> 00:02:14,441
Super, super convenient when we're racing Miatas

49
00:02:14,461 --> 00:02:16,121
and we need stuff on the fly.

50
00:02:16,141 --> 00:02:18,361
Long story short, he's got other things he could be doing,

51
00:02:18,381 --> 00:02:19,721
but he decided to just do this for fun.

52
00:02:19,741 --> 00:02:21,241
This is not his regular job.

53
00:02:21,261 --> 00:02:23,821
Yeah, let's bring this car back and start scanning it.

54
00:02:25,741 --> 00:02:28,201
All right, so we're going to scan this NB

55
00:02:28,221 --> 00:02:30,141
on the ground as it sits as a control.

56
00:02:30,621 --> 00:02:32,361
To see how much deflection we have.

57
00:02:32,381 --> 00:02:37,321
At the core of this test is our handy-dandy Artec Leo scanner.

58
00:02:37,341 --> 00:02:40,521
So what's going to happen is we're going to do a total of four scans.

59
00:02:40,541 --> 00:02:43,961
First set is going to be the car scanned bone stock on the ground.

60
00:02:43,981 --> 00:02:46,841
Second is we're going to jack up a corner to a very specific height

61
00:02:46,861 --> 00:02:48,441
and scan it again.

62
00:02:48,461 --> 00:02:50,921
We're going to then throw the strut tower brace

63
00:02:50,941 --> 00:02:53,801
and the fender brace separately on the car, scan it again.

64
00:02:53,821 --> 00:02:56,221
And then finally, the last scan is going to be

65
00:02:56,941 --> 00:02:59,561
the strut tower brace and the fender brace together.

66
00:02:59,581 --> 00:03:02,521
This will give us very good data to measure just how much

67
00:03:02,541 --> 00:03:04,521
each individual item does and what they do together.

68
00:03:04,541 --> 00:03:07,261
So let's get started and scan the factory car.

69
00:03:08,490 --> 00:03:10,020
All right, here's our control.

70
00:03:10,050 --> 00:03:11,890
Car on the ground, bone stock.

71
00:03:13,410 --> 00:03:15,190
What we're measuring is the width

72
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:16,400
across the engine bay,

73
00:03:16,430 --> 00:03:18,210
from one strut tower to the

74
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,410
other. On the ground,

75
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:22,130
that's 960.9 millimeters. That's our baseline.

76
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,640
So it's five scans total:

77
00:03:23,670 --> 00:03:25,450
this one, and the remaining four

78
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,950
with the car jacked up.

79
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:29,680
Now we jack up one front

80
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:31,550
corner to a very specific height,

81
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:33,420
and we check it with a

82
00:03:33,450 --> 00:03:35,290
tape measure so it's the same

83
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,160
every time. Lift one corner like

84
00:03:37,190 --> 00:03:39,030
this and you're twisting the whole

85
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:40,280
chassis. From here on,

86
00:03:40,310 --> 00:03:41,530
same corner, same height.

87
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:43,400
All we change is the bracing.

88
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:52,380
With no bracing, one corner in

89
00:03:52,410 --> 00:03:54,180
the air, and the strut towers

90
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:57,480
go from 960.9 to 962.6.

91
00:03:57,510 --> 00:03:59,590
That's 1.7 millimeters wider,

92
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:01,390
just from jacking up one corner.

93
00:04:02,270 --> 00:04:04,460
That 1.7 is the number the

94
00:04:04,490 --> 00:04:05,450
braces have to beat.

95
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:07,770
For the rest of the car,

96
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,230
we lay the jacked up scan

97
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:10,690
over the control scan and color

98
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:12,150
in what's different. Green and light

99
00:04:12,180 --> 00:04:13,370
blue is the small stuff,

100
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,580
a few millimeters either way.

101
00:04:14,610 --> 00:04:16,040
Yellow to red means it moved

102
00:04:16,070 --> 00:04:17,500
outward. Dark blue means it moved

103
00:04:17,530 --> 00:04:18,960
inward. And this scale goes out

104
00:04:18,990 --> 00:04:20,430
to fifteen millimeters, so it's not

105
00:04:20,460 --> 00:04:21,890
going to show you a millimeter

106
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:22,860
at the strut towers.

107
00:04:22,890 --> 00:04:24,320
That's what the measurement is for.

108
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,940
With no bracing, it moves a

109
00:04:26,970 --> 00:04:28,110
lot. On one side,

110
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:29,880
the door and the rear quarter

111
00:04:29,910 --> 00:04:31,650
go orange, so that's moving outward,

112
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:33,410
around six millimeters. Come around to

113
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:35,180
the other side, and the same

114
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:36,950
area goes blue. That's moving inward.

115
00:04:37,830 --> 00:04:39,450
One side in, the other side

116
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,110
out. That's what you'd expect from

117
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:42,220
a car that's twisting.

118
00:04:42,250 --> 00:04:43,880
Just keep in mind this is

119
00:04:43,910 --> 00:04:45,260
the outside of the car.

120
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:46,640
Doors, the top, the trunk,

121
00:04:46,670 --> 00:04:48,300
those can shift on their own.

122
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:49,960
Overall, by our own math on

123
00:04:49,990 --> 00:04:51,620
the scans, a little under sixty

124
00:04:51,650 --> 00:04:53,280
percent of the body is within

125
00:04:53,310 --> 00:04:55,490
two and a half millimeters of the control.

126
00:04:59,170 --> 00:05:00,640
First we're going to throw on

127
00:05:00,670 --> 00:05:02,140
the fender braces from Goodwin Racing.

128
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:03,640
The fender has to come off

129
00:05:03,670 --> 00:05:05,140
for these. They bolt in behind

130
00:05:05,170 --> 00:05:06,640
it, from the door hinge area

131
00:05:06,670 --> 00:05:07,640
down to the chassis,

132
00:05:07,670 --> 00:05:09,140
so they triangulate that whole corner.

133
00:05:09,170 --> 00:05:10,130
Then we scan it.

134
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:22,100
Then it's the same corner,

135
00:05:22,130 --> 00:05:23,600
same jack height, and we scan

136
00:05:23,630 --> 00:05:24,600
the engine bay again.

137
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:30,850
With just the fender braces,

138
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:33,210
the engine bay is only 0.3

139
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,520
millimeters wider than our control.

140
00:05:34,550 --> 00:05:36,890
With no bracing it was 1.7,

141
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,460
so by this measurement that's about

142
00:05:38,490 --> 00:05:39,250
eighty percent less.

143
00:05:40,130 --> 00:05:41,610
And the crazy part is,

144
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:44,020
these braces don't even touch the strut towers.

145
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:46,390
Here's no bracing on the left,

146
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:47,900
and the fender braces on the

147
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:49,160
right. The sides calm down.

148
00:05:49,190 --> 00:05:50,680
That orange door and that blue

149
00:05:50,710 --> 00:05:51,940
rear quarter are mostly gone.

150
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:53,840
But from the top,

151
00:05:53,870 --> 00:05:55,420
the trunk and the rear deck

152
00:05:55,450 --> 00:05:56,480
go yellow and orange,

153
00:05:56,510 --> 00:05:57,530
and they weren't before.

154
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,120
Why? Most likely because the front

155
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:00,700
of the car is stiffer now,

156
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:02,280
so more of that load gets

157
00:06:02,310 --> 00:06:03,340
transferred to the rear.

158
00:06:03,370 --> 00:06:04,920
Overall it's still about sixty percent

159
00:06:04,950 --> 00:06:06,500
of the body within two and

160
00:06:06,530 --> 00:06:07,290
a half millimeters.

161
00:06:10,970 --> 00:06:12,440
Next up is the strut tower

162
00:06:12,470 --> 00:06:13,940
brace by itself. No fender braces

163
00:06:13,970 --> 00:06:15,440
