189
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,920
of the body is within two

190
00:07:04,950 --> 00:07:06,000
and a half millimeters.

191
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:08,350
Out of the two braces by

192
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:09,850
themselves, this is the cleaner heat

193
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:11,350
map. My guess is the strut

194
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:12,840
tower brace is better at resisting

195
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:14,090
this specific kind of twist,

196
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:15,590
the kind you get from jacking

197
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:17,090
up one corner. But that's a

198
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,830
hypothesis. We would need to investigate more.

199
00:07:22,510 --> 00:07:24,090
And then the last scan.

200
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:26,010
Both the fender braces and the

201
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,940
strut tower brace on the car,

202
00:07:27,970 --> 00:07:29,220
jacked up and scanned.

203
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,630
With both braces on,

204
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:36,470
it's 0.5 millimeters wider than our

205
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,360
control, about seventy percent less than

206
00:07:38,390 --> 00:07:40,250
no bracing. Better than the strut

207
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:41,510
tower brace by itself.

208
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:43,720
Not better than just the fender braces.

209
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,070
Now, those two are only about

